From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MichaIng <micha@dietpi.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 17:30:00 +0100
Subject: arm64: dts: rockchip: Enable TSADC on NanoPi Zero2

The RK3528 TSADC node is disabled by default, which leaves the SoC
thermal zone without a sensor, so neither a thermal zone nor a hwmon
device is registered. Enable it on the NanoPi Zero2, like on the ROCK 2.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3528-nanopi-zero2.dts | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3528-nanopi-zero2.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3528-nanopi-zero2.dts
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3528-nanopi-zero2.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3528-nanopi-zero2.dts
@@ -344,6 +344,10 @@ &sdmmc {
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
+&tsadc {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
 &uart0 {
 	pinctrl-names = "default";
 	pinctrl-0 = <&uart0m0_xfer>;
-- 
Armbian

